        "text": "DEMO EVIDENCE UPDATE · PRESENTATION 338 / SOURCE 331\nThe background carries most of the measured quality cost.\ndk2 author result · provisional · existing clips\n\nSwapping regions between plain Nano and Nano-Phys localizes about 70% of the fused DOVER drop to the background on this grid. This is an attribution through a learned visual-quality metric.\n\n36 existing task-276 clips · 6 takes of one pendulum rig × seeds 1–3 · 2×2 region swaps · identical x264 CRF 12 encoding · 3 DOVER repetitions on an RTX 4060.\n\nBACKGROUND EFFECT · FUSED DOVER\n−0.0446\n\nSource 95% interval [−0.0532, −0.0371]\n18/18 paired effects below zero. About 70% of the total −0.0641 in the re-encoded set.\n\nSENSITIVITY CONTROL · PLAIN CLIPS\n−0.077\n\nAuthor reports this DOVER change after Gaussian blur with σ = 0.5 pixels. A −1.5-grey offset costs −0.026. Neither control measures physics or establishes human perceptual equivalence.\n\nCompare only within the re-encoded set. Re-encoding itself shifts fused DOVER by −0.019 for plain and −0.026 for Nano-Phys. The earlier task-319 drop of −0.057 uses the original files; it is a separate comparison.\n\nThe two branches tell different stories\nDOVER metric\nFused\nAesthetic\nTechnical\n\nBackground: 69.5% of total · corridor: 30.5%. Different metric branches have different scales.\n\nTotal\n−0.0641 [−0.0773, −0.0558]\n18/18 negative\nBackground\n−0.0446 [−0.0532, −0.0371]\n18/18 negative\nCorridor\n−0.0195 [−0.0262, −0.0129]\n16/18 negative\nInteraction\n−0.0084 [−0.0169, −0.0019]\n11/18 negative\n\nBar lengths show absolute magnitudes within the selected metric; values retain their signs. Intervals are copied from the source JSON. Main effects average over the other region's source. They sum to the total; interaction is a separate difference-of-differences, not an extra cost to add.\n\nThe source README and board call the bootstrap “exact,” but the pinned analysis script uses 20,000 Monte Carlo draws of six take means (random seed 0). We preserve the saved intervals and flag this label discrepancy. These intervals are conditional on the six takes and shared seeds; they do not cover new rigs, prompts, or all scorer variation.\n\nExplore the four saved scores for each pair\n\nSelect a take and seed. First letter = corridor source; second = background source. P = plain, N = Nano-Phys. The region drawings below are symbolic, not masks or video frames.\n\nInput take\n09\n12\n16\n17\n18\n19\nSeed\n1\n2\n3\nPP · corridor plain\nbackground plain\ncorridor\n0.58932\nsaved fused score\nNP · corridor Nano-Phys\nbackground plain\ncorridor\n0.56890\nsaved fused score\nPN · corridor plain\nbackground Nano-Phys\ncorridor\n0.50044\nsaved fused score\nNN · corridor Nano-Phys\nbackground Nano-Phys\ncorridor\n0.44964\nsaved fused score\n\nTake 09, seed 1: total −0.1397 · background −0.1041 · corridor −0.0356 · interaction −0.0304.\n\nSource feathered-mask area: 33.0% of this frame; same mask used for its four cells.\n\nTake / seed\tPP\tNN\tNP\tPN\tTotal\tBackground\tCorridor\n09 / 1\t0.58932\t0.44964\t0.56890\t0.50044\t-0.13969\t-0.10407\t-0.03562\n09 / 2\t0.49508\t0.41777\t0.48655\t0.46243\t-0.07731\t-0.05071\t-0.02659\n09 / 3\t0.51173\t0.44129\t0.48962\t0.48273\t-0.07044\t-0.03866\t-0.03177\n12 / 1\t0.57121\t0.49174\t0.56329\t0.49694\t-0.07947\t-0.07291\t-0.00656\n12 / 2\t0.49312\t0.45852\t0.48440\t0.46420\t-0.03460\t-0.02740\t-0.00720\n12 / 3\t0.53611\t0.46557\t0.51658\t0.50902\t-0.07054\t-0.03905\t-0.03149\n16 / 1\t0.52332\t0.42643\t0.49722\t0.46547\t-0.09688\t-0.06431\t-0.03257\n16 / 2\t0.44195\t0.41265\t0.42818\t0.44592\t-0.02930\t-0.00578\t-0.02352\n16 / 3\t0.46268\t0.40858\t0.43398\t0.44190\t-0.05410\t-0.02309\t-0.03101\n17 / 1\t0.57190\t0.49355\t0.57696\t0.49006\t-0.07835\t-0.08262\t0.00427\n17 / 2\t0.50730\t0.46367\t0.49091\t0.47243\t-0.04363\t-0.03106\t-0.01257\n17 / 3\t0.52575\t0.49090\t0.52251\t0.50260\t-0.03485\t-0.02738\t-0.00747\n18 / 1\t0.61194\t0.50749\t0.58611\t0.53316\t-0.10445\t-0.07870\t-0.02575\n18 / 2\t0.51336\t0.46387\t0.49872\t0.49116\t-0.04948\t-0.02852\t-0.02096\n18 / 3\t0.52866\t0.50456\t0.51656\t0.50739\t-0.02410\t-0.01663\t-0.00746\n19 / 1\t0.55337\t0.46458\t0.53360\t0.47752\t-0.08879\t-0.07244\t-0.01635\n19 / 2\t0.51049\t0.45624\t0.47593\t0.50693\t-0.05425\t-0.01162\t-0.04263\n19 / 3\t0.49785\t0.47375\t0.49891\t0.46791\t-0.02411\t-0.02755\t0.00345\n\nAll 18 pairs remain visible. No measurement gate or human quality judgment is added by this table.\n\nWhat the controls support\nSimple tone matching did not recover the gap: matching each arm's static background to its input frame leaves −0.062 DOVER [−0.076, −0.053], as reported by dk2. This tested offset correction does not establish that all photometric effects are absent.\nFine-detail loss is a candidate: source background PSNR is 34.4 dB for plain versus 33.7 for Nano-Phys; Laplacian-variance ratios are 0.82 versus 0.80. This does not isolate a VAE, compression, proxy, or sampling cause.\nMask and seam dependence: the corridor unions pixels changing from frame 0 in plain, Nano-Phys, and proxy videos (threshold 25 grey; 3×3 opening, 21-pixel dilation, Gaussian feather σ 6). It covers 20–49% of the image and can include other moving content. Compositing seams can affect scores; the interaction term does not separately identify a seam contribution.\nScope: one rig, repeated takes, fixed shared seeds, generated 93 frames at 24 fps and 832×480, CFG 6, 35 steps, supplied proxy at σ ≈ 0.898. The source records later-real-video periods. No new clips or scores were produced for this page.\nNot established: a first-frame-only physics remedy, general human visual improvement, judge or robot-prediction non-regression, or the cause of the texture change. Planted-case validation does not apply to this visual-quality score.\nFIX UNDER TEST BY EXPERIMENT OWNERS\nRestrict proxy guidance to the motion region\n\nRegion-wise latent noising and stochastic flow relaxation are published methods. Tasks 336/337 coordinate their Nano-Phys test. This page contains no result for that fix. The pixel-level region swap is a diagnostic, not an inference recipe.\n\nSuggested demo copy\n“On six pendulum takes × three seeds, a region-swap analysis attributes about 70% of Nano-Phys' re-encoded DOVER loss to the background. A simple tone correction does not recover it, and DOVER is sensitive to small blur. The underlying cause and a remedy remain under test.”\n\nHuman-applied wording proposal. Earlier period-transfer and quality cards remain separate: original quality scorecard · fresh-input outcomes · supplied-state demo.\n\nAttribution and receipts\n\nAnalysis and scores: dk2, task 331 / finding #6767, pinned commit e36f89c. Presentation: ro-sol1, task 338. This packaging does not independently replicate scoring or physical measurement.\n\nPlain-text readout · SHA256 receipts · Board messages · Packaging validation · Browser validation · Separate gallery HTTP observations\n\nAll 13 exact source snapshots\nPublished context read before this task\n\nStatic local readout. Deployment and gallery service changes remain with their owners. Judged root README and reports are untouched.",
